※ pl4g-test: compile=ok opt=0,1 run=native,qemu exit=90 diag=none

※ The same function with `a` written for `⎕entry(a)`, which is a different
※ question and a false one: the name stands for what the parameter is at the
※ return, so `⎕answer > a` asks whether six is more than six.
※
※ That the two differ is the whole reason `⎕entry` exists, and it is what this
※ pair of tests is for.

@[inline(never)]
fn bump(a: mut u8) → u8 post(⎕answer > a):
    a ← a ⊞ 1u8
    a

@[startup]
fn main() → u6:
    ⎕narrow(bump(5u8), ⌜u6⌝) ?? 1u6
